1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,250
I'm Zoe.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:03,790
Prize organizers may need to fund Bitcoin

3
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:05,430
before they know the winner,

4
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:07,550
or the winner’s Bitcoin address.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,860
PrizeKey lets you fund Bitcoin now,

6
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:12,080
and choose the recipient later.

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,450
In this recorded testnet run,

8
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,820
I create a gift.

9
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,900
It gets its own Bitcoin address

10
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,150
and a transferable claim on NEAR.

11
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,350
The gift is funded with 20,000 test sats.

12
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,450
I enter the winner’s NEAR account

13
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:26,970
and transfer the claim.

14
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:29,000
Ownership has changed.

15
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,950
The new holder chooses a Bitcoin destination

16
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:34,100
and authorizes the payout

17
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,010
through NEAR Chain Signatures.

18
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,580
The browser broadcasts the signed Bitcoin transaction.

19
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,000
No wrapped token,

20
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,330
and no private key passed to the winner.

21
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,840
The public Bitcoin record confirms

22
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:49,400
19,750 test sats delivered,

23
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,280
with a 250-sat fee.

24
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,560
This is a testnet prototype

25
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:56,800
with an admin upgrade key.

26
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,600
Fund first, pass the claim,

27
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,460
and let the holder choose where Bitcoin goes.
